---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Kirpik is built by INFOWISE LIMITED, the team behind Tilkie image protection, to give Shopify merchants a workable way to prove ownership of their own writing."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About"
    title="Made for merchants who write their own copy."
    lead="Kirpik exists for a small, specific injustice: the person who wrote the product description losing out to the person who pasted it."
  />

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <h2>Why we built it</h2>
      <p>
        Good product copy takes real work. Research, drafts, the tenth rewrite
        of the opening line. Copying it takes a keyboard shortcut, and on
        Shopify it does not even take that, because every store publishes its
        product text in feeds designed for software to read. The apps sold as
        the answer mostly disable right-click, which inconveniences customers
        and does nothing to a scraper.
      </p>
      <p>
        We took a different position: you cannot stop text from being copied,
        so make every copy traceable. Kirpik embeds an invisible watermark in
        your descriptions, articles and pages, without changing your words,
        and when your writing turns up somewhere else, it gives you detection
        and a Chain of Proof certificate instead of a shrug.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Kirpik is developed by {SITE.developer}. We are a small team that
        builds practical software for merchants, and we hold ourselves to the
        same standard on this site: no invented statistics, no fake reviews,
        and no claims the product cannot back up. Where Kirpik has limits, we
        say so in plain terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Kirpik and Tilkie</h2>
      <p>
        Kirpik has a sibling. <a href="https://tilkie.app" rel="noopener">Tilkie</a>
        does for product images what Kirpik does for text: an invisible
        watermark, detection, and a Chain of Proof certificate for the day a
        copy appears. The two apps share a developer and a philosophy, and
        stores that get scraped for one usually get scraped for both.
      </p>

      <h2>Talk to us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, bug reports and blunt feedback are all welcome. The
        <a href="/support/">Support page</a> lists the ways to reach us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</Base>
